# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .` in the FINAL stage, so anything not excluded here is baked into
# the published image. That is what makes this file load-bearing rather than a build-speed tweak.
#
# `.claude/` is the pointed one: this is a public repo whose Claude memory is deliberately
# local-only (git-ignored via .git/info/exclude, never committed). Without this entry a LOCAL
# `docker build` would copy that memory -- session logs, audit reports, STATE.md -- straight into
# an image layer, bypassing every git-side control that keeps it out of the repo. CI is unaffected,
# because it builds from a fresh checkout where `.claude/` does not exist; the exposure is the day
# someone builds and pushes from a working copy.

# Claude / workbench memory -- see above. Local-only by policy; must never reach an image.
.claude
CLAUDE.md

# VCS and CI
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# Local data and generated artifacts. Large, machine-specific, and regenerated at runtime.
data
models
results
logs

# Python build and cache noise
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.venv
venv

# Tests do not run in the image
tests

# Editor and OS
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store

# Env files: the image takes configuration from the environment, not from a baked-in file.
.env
.env.*

# Docs
README.md
LICENSE
